<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1451bde38cbe2f2f8fcd98c9cc24a81ae18c634d" commit="1ef7cb29bcc6d5eddac5fcf3a10b507c3a03ede6" commit_message="chromeos-base: remove glbench ebuild  This version (source code under platform2/glbench) is based on X11 and is deprecated. The actual glbench source code used by autotest lives under autotest/files/client/deps/glbench/.  BUG=none TEST=none  Change-Id: I1451bde38cbe2f2f8fcd98c9cc24a81ae18c634d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/390324 Commit-Ready: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="390324" owner_email="hshi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/24/390324/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If9b51c59a7edbcb892ec86a687a41d63db8e4f1a" commit="3b5909ff8c82cbb03745cc114ec7ab10270e2298" commit_message="glbench/images: remove all files under glbench/images  This repository is defunct. The actual images in use are under autotest/files/client/deps/glbench-images/  BUG=none TEST=none CQ-DEPEND=CL:390324  Change-Id: If9b51c59a7edbcb892ec86a687a41d63db8e4f1a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/390360 Commit-Ready: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ilja H. Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="390360" owner_email="hshi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/glbench/images" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/glbench/images" ref="refs/changes/60/390360/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If2191d098b3d6ed32f9fb668368b42e6697b9ff1" commit="ae358d64b901c955f7e05cf7f669e783948c3029" commit_message="Remove glbench/images under platform2/.  This repository is defunct. The actual images in use are under autotest/files/client/deps/glbench-images/  BUG=none TEST=none CQ-DEPEND=CL:390360  Change-Id: If2191d098b3d6ed32f9fb668368b42e6697b9ff1 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/390503 Commit-Ready: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="390503" owner_email="hshi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/manifest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/manifest" ref="refs/changes/03/390503/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1d715c22779226937546e0566dceb0de29501b60" commit="c159d286e58c973eccb80515f6517de6341ae31f" commit_message="login: Explicitly remount the container with MS_RDONLY  Turns out that even if the filesystem is mounted read-only outside the container, the same mount inside the container will preserve the flag that was passed explicitly (0, meaning read-write), even if the underlying filesystem was marked read-only.  This change explicitly remounts the containers' rootfs with MS_RDONLY if the underlying filesystem is mounted read-only.  BUG=b:31771616 TEST=FEATURES=&quot;test&quot; emerge-${BOARD} chromeos-base/chromeos-login TEST=test_that cheets_FileSystemPermission  # passes TEST=test_that cheets_FileSystemPermission  # fails with WRITABLE_MOUNT=1  Change-Id: I1d715c22779226937546e0566dceb0de29501b60 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/390412 Commit-Ready: Luis Hector Chavez &lt;lhchavez@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Luis Hector Chavez &lt;lhchavez@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Luis Hector Chavez &lt;lhchavez@google.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="390412" owner_email="lhchavez@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/12/390412/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I922710079ac5f4c9ca9c177eab880a99ada1415e" commit="0ceb75bc187d9fe9ec9d3f60f7a22881b1e879be" commit_message="syslinux: drop local copy  We have a newer version in portage-stable now we want to use.  Keep in mind that syslinux is not used on any official Chrome OS device as we have our own custom firmware everywhere.  It is only used when booting Chromium OS.  Our copy had a few custom changes: - Turn off the video cursor before booting the kernel - Sometimes disable display of the syslinux banner when booting - Disable display of all info messages  The first patch is no longer needed: our boot splash code takes care of turning off the cursor before showing the screen, either directly (when USE=vtconsole), or by letting frecon do it when it creates the new VT.  Disabling the boot banner happens only for some boot paths (e.g. the isolinux code), but not all (e.g. the serial port), and it disables only part of the banner.  It also doesn't disable all messages that come up early on.  In the end, it doesn't make things all the much more quiet to the point where we need to maintain it.  The code also tried to disable the common writemsg function, but it is only called for info/debug messages, none of which are displayed by default.  Which means it's kind of a pointless change.  By dropping our custom syslinux version, we make the output a little bit more verbose for Chromium OS builds, but since we aren't silent now, it's not a big deal.  BUG=chromium:508713 TEST=`emerge syslinux` uses the new one in portage-stable TEST=vmtests pass CQ-DEPEND=CL:382771  Change-Id: I922710079ac5f4c9ca9c177eab880a99ada1415e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/382772 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@google.com&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="382772" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/72/382772/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-5.39" change_id="I2da6b486964553b11d88796719bf074419daccde" commit="e9dff4aa15f44b88af00f71ff1ae5309d642ce14" commit_message="UPSTREAM: client: Show UUIDs when listing attributes  Example output after this patch:  [bluetooth]# connect 7B:3F:2C:2B:D0:06 Attempting to connect to 7B:3F:2C:2B:D0:06 [CHG] Device 7B:3F:2C:2B:D0:06 Connected: yes Connection successful [NEW] Primary Service         /org/bluez/hci0/dev_7B_3F_2C_2B_D0_06/service0001         00001801-0000-1000-8000-00805f9b34fb         Generic Attribute Profile [NEW] Characteristic         /org/bluez/hci0/dev_7B_3F_2C_2B_D0_06/service0001/char0002         00002a05-0000-1000-8000-00805f9b34fb         Service Changed [NEW] Primary Service         /org/bluez/hci0/dev_7B_3F_2C_2B_D0_06/service0028         0000180f-0000-1000-8000-00805f9b34fb         Battery Service [NEW] Characteristic         /org/bluez/hci0/dev_7B_3F_2C_2B_D0_06/service0028/char0029         00002a19-0000-1000-8000-00805f9b34fb         Battery Level [NEW] Descriptor         /org/bluez/hci0/dev_7B_3F_2C_2B_D0_06/service0028/char0029/desc002b         00002902-0000-1000-8000-00805f9b34fb         Client Characteristic Configuration [CHG] Device 7B:3F:2C:2B:D0:06 UUIDs: 00001800-0000-1000-8000-00805f9b34fb [CHG] Device 7B:3F:2C:2B:D0:06 UUIDs: 00001801-0000-1000-8000-00805f9b34fb [CHG] Device 7B:3F:2C:2B:D0:06 UUIDs: 0000180f-0000-1000-8000-00805f9b34fb [CHG] Device 7B:3F:2C:2B:D0:06 ServicesResolved: yes  BUG=none TEST=build  Change-Id: I2da6b486964553b11d88796719bf074419daccde Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/388974 Commit-Ready: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: François Beaufort &lt;fbeaufort@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="388974" owner_email="mcchou@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/bluez" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/bluez" ref="refs/changes/74/388974/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie9e1b0ccbf76e1cbcacbbe9737797dbac6559ef8" commit="c84f376b32fd7cdc1465999259267d0a365fb888" commit_message="[autotest] Update servo_host update to work with labstation as well.  Added a new AFE rpc (retrieve_hosts_by_host_attribute) that returns a list of dut hostnames that all share the same host attribute values (helper function to find all duts using the same servo host).  Added a new context manager to lock duts to ensure no duts will be impacted while rebooting the servo host.  Added a new test servohost_Reboot to handle a synchronized reboot for a servo host.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:388674 BUG=chromium:599533 TEST=locally on moblab with 2 duts with the labstation primed for a reboot.  Checked that: - no more than 1 servohost_Reboot test got scheduled. - servohost_Reboot waited for the locked dut to go idle before rebooting   the servo host. - all duts were unlocked regardless of failure in servohost_Reboot.  Change-Id: Ie9e1b0ccbf76e1cbcacbbe9737797dbac6559ef8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/375961 Commit-Ready: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="375961" owner_email="kevcheng@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="11" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/61/375961/11" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie51f9a23575c2afd21adf0e91fbbdd98a9362d05" commit="33fcdf4fbc9585f1172a7637ec7257d12b1d5318" commit_message="upload_symbols.py: Improve upload failure error messages  Existing message was causing some confusion about what was being skipped. Broken error message into 2.  BUG=chromium:647101 TEST=scripts/upload_symbols_unittest  Change-Id: Ie51f9a23575c2afd21adf0e91fbbdd98a9362d05 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/390353 Commit-Ready: Chris Ching &lt;chingcodes@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Chris Ching &lt;chingcodes@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="390353" owner_email="chingcodes@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/53/390353/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I71e4fa8f21ade96db69011aac29f922ac6b9e424" commit="3d2a4e8f2d23661ba8f52de0821469f3b7dff077" commit_message="libcontainer: create cgroups with container's gid  In order for the container to be able to manipulate passed cgroups (Android wants to change ownership of some objects, inclusing tasks attribute, to be system:system) we need to ensure that not only user switched to the container owner, but group as well.  BUG=chromium:647994 TEST=boot ocntainer, check that /dev/cpuset belongs to system:system  Change-Id: I71e4fa8f21ade96db69011aac29f922ac6b9e424 Signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/390355 Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="390355" owner_email="dtor@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/55/390355/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I42c04f2fdecf8e6d595703e45d90f6ba7ede3721" commit="82ba49e3b2283ff4a5447c2b50c914514489086a" commit_message="cros_ec_dev: Fix device path buffer  The buffer which stores the path of the CrOS EC device was re-factored improperly when non-EC device support was added, causing a buffer overflow which was exposed when flashrom is compiled using clang.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:57950 BRANCH=none TEST=&quot;flashrom -p ec -w ec.bin&quot; no longer crashes when flashrom is built using clang  Change-Id: I42c04f2fdecf8e6d595703e45d90f6ba7ede3721 Signed-off-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/390379 Reviewed-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="390379" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/79/390379/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3fe0bb17a757f94fa18100d1811af6f8fecba83b" commit="9e323b44c64dc30eb15f4355da6cbb0e0a4e250a" commit_message="[autotest] Add backwards compatibility wrapper for ts_mon config  If ts_mon_config.SetupTsMonGlobalState() is not a context manager, we need to return a trivial context manager to allow using the result in a with: statement. This can happen if we are using an old version of chromite, such as in Moblab.  BUG=b:31809563 TEST=Running a Moblab tryjob  Change-Id: I3fe0bb17a757f94fa18100d1811af6f8fecba83b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/390327 Commit-Ready: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: John Carey &lt;ranix@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="390327" owner_email="phobbs@google.com" pass_count="0"