_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/15/381015/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.10" change_id="I7b1ed72c222e7345b24071ea8cc45fbffaeb7c02" commit="f4d9bad0757d90c54a2e512c68f75341c827fe8e" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/tegra: implement save/restore for Tegra connector  Tegra connector hotplug handlers usually call drm_helper_hpd_irq_event to send uevent. However the drm_helper_hpd_irq_event holds the lock mode_config.mutex which is also needed for Tegra DRM suspend/resume. Once the hotplug happens during suspend/resume, Tegra DRM suspend/resume process could be blocked by drm_helper_hpd_irq_event due to lock contension. Given during system suspend/resume we don't really care about connector hotplug events, this patch implements save/restore routines for Tegra connectors and uses them to ignore hotplug events conditionally.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:56391 TEST=no reboot occurred during system resume with HDMI connected  Change-Id: I7b1ed72c222e7345b24071ea8cc45fbffaeb7c02 Signed-off-by: Vince Hsu &lt;vince.h@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/381036 Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mark Zhang &lt;markz@gpartner-nvidia.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="381036" owner_email="vince.h@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/36/381036/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I39f3f6914fe49b7671d621169b90a7c08fc0c20e" commit="52310b0f7b1f0171a6d24943cb2cbccca2fb2fb0" commit_message="Add FW update check flow when firmware is in bootloader  The script will check the firmware status, If the touchscreen is in boot mode, it will skip hardware vers